s input for an encoding task. The mismatched title and description are a clear quality and trust warning.</p></article><article class="min-w-0 rounded-card border border-border bg-paper-raised/40 px-5 py-4"><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><h3 class="min-w-0 font-display text-base font-semibold leading-snug"><a href="/servers/com-jojapi-tiktok-download-video" class="break-words text-ink no-underline hover:text-dead">tiktok-download-video</a> <span class="meta-mono ml-1 break-all !normal-case">com.jojapi/tiktok-download-video</span></h3><span class="stamp stamp-dead " style="transform:rotate(-0.7deg)">Flagged</span></div><p class="mt-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">This server appears to provide a TikTok video download/API service with a free monthly quota. It is likely aimed at developers or media workflows that need TikTok content retrieval. The description is promotional, oddly truncated, and keyword-stuffed, which is a clear quality concern for a curated directory.</p></article><article class="min-w-0 rounded-card border border-border bg-paper-raised/40 px-5 py-4"><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><h3 class="min-w-0 font-display text-base font-semibold leading-snug"><a href="/servers/dev-workers-pathwren-www-robots-policy-lint" class="break-words text-ink no-underline hover:text-dead">Robots.txt Policy Lint</a> <span class="meta-mono ml-1 break-all !normal-case">dev.workers.pathwren.www/robots-policy-lint</span></h3><span class="stamp stamp-dead " style="transform:rotate(0.6000000000000001deg)">Flagged</span></div><p class="mt-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">This is supposed to lint robots.txt policy, which would normally be useful for SEO, crawling, or compliance checks. The listing metadata is the problem: the description is a pasted JSON-RPC call with &quot;free no key&quot; appended, which looks l