etadata and keyword-heavy branding is a bad-faith signal strong enough to warrant caution.</p></article><article class="min-w-0 rounded-card border border-border bg-paper-raised/40 px-5 py-4"><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><h3 class="min-w-0 font-display text-base font-semibold leading-snug"><a href="/servers/io-github-webformike-citerank" class="break-words text-ink no-underline hover:text-dead">CiteRank MCP</a> <span class="meta-mono ml-1 break-all !normal-case">io.github.WebforMike/citerank</span></h3><span class="stamp stamp-dead " style="transform:rotate(-0.30000000000000004deg)">Flagged</span></div><p class="mt-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A remote-only audit server framed around AI visibility, citations, agentic readiness, agent journeys, and WordPress deployment in one package. It appears targeted at SEO and marketing operators trying to optimize sites for AI-discovery narratives. The description is heavily buzzword-loaded and reads more like keyword stuffing than a well-bounded product definition, which is a bad-faith signal for a curated directory.</p></article><article class="min-w-0 rounded-card border border-border bg-paper-raised/40 px-5 py-4"><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><h3 class="min-w-0 font-display text-base font-semibold leading-snug"><a href="/servers/com-promtpress-ads" class="break-words text-ink no-underline hover:text-dead">ads</a> <span class="meta-mono ml-1 break-all !normal-case">com.promtpress/ads</span></h3><span class="stamp stamp-dead " style="transform:rotate(0.8999999999999999deg)">Flagged</span></div><p class="mt-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">This server appears to sell Telegram subscribers and website traffic on a pay-per-result basis. It is aimed at growth hacking or traffic acquisition rather than legitimate developer workflows, and the description raises